stray the game that lets you finally  live every gamer's dream of being a  kitty in a cyberpunk world is nearly  upon us so to prepare you for the latest  game from renowned publisher annapurna  interactive and developer blue12 studios  here's everything you need to know about  stray  [Music]  stray puts you into the furry paws of a  cat traveling through a dystopian blade  runner-esque world populated solely by  robots not much is known about the  game's mysterious plot but as the cat  you'll explore the long forgotten cyber  city in order to uncover a strange  mystery and find your way home to your  family on your journey you'll encounter  and interact with the robo-denizens of  this strange world eventually being able  to communicate with them  in terms of gameplay stray like our  feline friends in general defies simple  explanation being a mashup of  platforming exploration and puzzle  solving it's also a cat simulator which  we all know is the main reason you're  gonna play this game first and foremost  though the game comes with a dedicated  button that lets you meow so don't worry  the game has you covered there you can  even do it during cinematics truly  putting you into the mindset of a cat  who doesn't care for such arbitrary  concerns like story and plot  but more importantly while the game does  contain platforming elements most of the  jumping and hopping around is made more  by button prompts rather than player  control as you explore the city the real  focus is on having you explore that city  with the challenge coming from figuring  out where to go rather than how to  navigate it initially the game's levels  start pretty straightforward and linear  but also contain more open-ended larger  segments for your feline form to explore  and uncover where you need to go further  straight contains puzzle elements  forcing you to try to figure out how to  navigate through its world such as  pushing over plants as every cat does or  utilizing pulley systems to access new  areas however these exploration and  navigation segments are not all  lackadaisical at certain points in the  game you'll be put into a chase sequence  forcing you to time exactly when you  need to take a path at the same time you  won't be able to engage in combat so  your only choice will be to escape this  leads to a need to think quickly and  make precise choices in the moment all  this adds pressure to your decisions and  amps up the adrenaline or catnip rush  however all this is done in service of  the game's world as you move throughout  the city you'll encounter more of the  robots inhabiting it eventually you'll  even be able to talk to them once you  get access to a robot companion named  b12 who can translate for you b12 an  adorable flying drone friend will also  help you navigate the city and help you  figure out where to go next you'll even  be able to take on quests and tasks from  the citizens adding in more complexity  to your exploration and you'll want to  explore this world because all of the  robot citizens as well as this cyber  city are extraordinarily pretty and well  animated further the world and your  place in it are shrouded in mystery  leading you to wonder where exactly this  story takes place the far future a  post-apocalypse another universe are all  part of your feline dreams furthermore  you'll have to answer the question  what happened to all the humans who else  is going to give you head scritches just  the way you like them all in all stray  seems to be a unique gaming experience  that draws from a variety of indie and  unique games like it takes to or inside  sadly as is befitting the independent  nature of our feline friend there is no  multiplayer announced for stray on top  of that there is currently no dlc  announced either meaning stray's 7 to 10  hour experience is all that we get for  now  [Music]  stray is currently a playstation console  exclusive meaning that xbox gamers will  sadly not be able to snag a copy  hopefully they're more dog people stray  will be coming to the playstation 4 and  5 via the playstation store however if  you don't own a playstation console you  can still pick it up on windows with it  already available for pre-order on steam  where it currently is one of the most  wish listed games of all time just shows  you that everybody wants to be a cat  because a cat's the only cat who knows  where it's at  stray is releasing on july 19 2022 and  will only be available digitally at full  price it currently retails at 29.99  however if you pre-order the game on  steam before july 19th you'll get a 10  discount making the game only 26.99  if you'd rather have the game for  playstation but don't want to pay the  full 29.99  you're also in luck stray will be  available for members of the extra  deluxe and premium tiers on playstation  plus at launch sadly if you only have  playstation plus essential you won't be  able to access the game for free  playstation plus extra tier is available  for 14.99 a month and the premium tier  is 17.99 a month bill lux is available  in markets outside of the united states  and its pricing varies based on location  and that's everything you need to know  before you can jump into the cyberpunk  world of our feline friend in stray we  recently had the chance to attend a  preview of stray so check out that video  for more information about the utter  cuteness of this game until then though  don't forget to like and subscribe and  make sure to stay out of the catnip  [Music]
 

